  "what_is_owed": "the frame cannot today tell these apart on its own. It is recorded here rather than parsed out of the error text, because that text is a Python repr the batch happened to write and reading it would be a guess dressed as a measurement.",
  "why_this_block_exists": "The frame reads a failed attempt as ROUTE_IMPLEMENTED_ATTEMPT_FAILED, which is the right name for an attempt that stopped - but it does not say whether what stopped it was a gap in this repository or a defect in the route. Both failures here are the first kind, and counting them with the other is how a source gap reads as an unexplained failure.",
  "why_this_shape_appears_at_all": "C02 is the first metric in this frame whose second source is needed to PREPARE the Run's input. C04's missing index is needed to resolve the metric, so its Run exists and the result is WITHHELD; C02's missing proxy means there is no input, and manufacturing a Run would mean declaring an input that does not exist. So the same kind of gap surfaces two different ways, and the difference is where in the route it is reached, not how serious it is."
 },
